# Mirrors asr-eval/.gitignore, for the same reasons. The split is: the EVAL SET is
# committed, MODEL OUTPUT never is.

# TTS response cache, keyed by sha256(text|voice|rate|pitch). Regenerable, and large.
cache/

# The QA JSON each arm produced. Model output, the same class the repo-root .gitignore
# keeps out for out/. Aggregates in reports/ are the shareable form.
hypotheses/

# Each ASR arm's transcripts. Model output over audio -- exactly what
# asr-eval/.gitignore excludes as hypotheses/, under a different directory name because
# here the ASR stage is an intermediate rather than the thing under test.
asr/

# audio/ IS committed, deliberately. Neural TTS is not bit-reproducible, so re-rendering
# produces perceptually identical files with different sha256 values. Freezing the wavs is
# the only thing that makes two arms comparable on identical bytes -- the same argument
# asr-eval/.gitignore makes for its own audio/.
